            0.783,
            0.107,
            0.839,
            0.123
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.772,
            0.132,
            0.935,
            0.427
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the force of friction is zero, a net force will have to be applied to an object at rest to set it moving. But once the object is moving, no further force is required to keep it moving with a constant velocity. However, to change the velocity (magnitude or direction), or to stop a moving object, a force will have to be applied."
            }
          ]
        },
