            0.193,
            0.635,
            0.384,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pause and Ponder"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.663,
            0.793,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. An object is moving with a constant velocity. Is there a net force acting upon it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.683,
            0.846,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Suppose, no net force is acting on an object. Which of the following situations are possible?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.717,
            0.436,
            0.734
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Object remains at rest if at rest."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.144,
            0.736,
            0.696,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Object keeps moving with a constant velocity if already moving."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.755,
            0.553,
            0.772
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Object is moving with a constant acceleration."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.774,
            0.846,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. In the real world, it is difficult to find a situation where no forces are acting on an object. But by applying additional forces, a condition can be achieved where the net force on the object is zero. Explain with the help of an example."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.854,
            0.74,
            0.923
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Newton’s first law of motion describes the motion of objects in the absence of a net force. It is natural to ask what happens to the motion of an object when there is a net force acting upon it. Newton’s second law of motion addresses this issue."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
